      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{x^{5}+7}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\nAssume $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x^{5}+7}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(x^{3} + \\frac{7}{x^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int x^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+7\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right)+7\\left(\\frac{x^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{4}}{4}-\\frac{7}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
