      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{f(x)}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\frac{2x^{2}-4}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(2 - \\frac{4}{x^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x-4\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)-4\\left(\\frac{x^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C \\\\ &=2x+\\frac{4}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe blank excludes the constant $C$, which is already supplied.",
